<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss building permits fall 2.5 pct in 10 months.</title>
<headline>Swiss building permits fall 2.5 pct in 10 months.</headline>
<dateline>SCHLIEREN, Switzerland 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Applications for building permits fell 2.5 percent to 19,626 in the first 10 months of 1996 from the same 1995 period, the Swiss Building Information Centre (MVS) said.</p>
<p>Applications for new buildings fell 0.4 percent from 1995 with a rise of 2.5 percent seen in the French-speaking part of Switzerland, a 0.1 percent decline in the German-speaking region and a 17.8 percent plunge in the Italian part.</p>
<p>Applications for residential buildings were down 0.2 percent in the first 10 months from last year.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
